(Stage 1b — inference soundness flip. A function with an UNDECLARED return
 type (`Return x add 1.` — no `a number,` prefix) is genuinely opaque to
 the compiler: its result is actually an integer, but the static default
 is now "mixed is the default", so appending it widens the list to Mixed.
 Reads dispatch on runtime tags; the string element proves dispatch is
 live — a fast-path int list would print "hello"'s pointer, not "hello".
 Acceptance criterion 3.)

